{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 377 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "1ff6beb5ca055acd486c384a842d72bed5bf3f16f9becadc12a3729217cbbb1b" :edb/db-before-t 376 :edb/db-after-t 377 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533689 50 #inst "2026-10-04T16:53:17.151Z" 13194139533689 true] [17592186054518 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247053 13194139533689 true] [17592186054662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247036 13194139533689 true] [17592186059606 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247046 13194139533689 true] [17592186059717 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247019 13194139533689 true] [17592186059769 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247060 13194139533689 true] [17592186068682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247012 13194139533689 true] [17592186073655 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247026 13194139533689 true] [17592186078378 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247039 13194139533689 true] [17592186087768 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247031 13194139533689 true] [17592186247012 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247013 13194139533689 true] [17592186247012 1089 "q-113303" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247012 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533689 true] [17592186247012 1100 "Simplify $\\frac{5}{2-h}-\\frac{3}{g(2-h)}.$" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247012 1113 #uuid "a972fb26-dd70-56b1-a8a0-8546890c476e" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247012 1138 false 13194139533689 true] [17592186247012 1145 "In order to subtract the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. Here, we can put both fractions over a common denominator of $g(2-h)$ if we multiply the top and bottom of the first fraction by $g:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2-h}-\\frac{3}{g(2-h)} & = \\\\ \\frac{g}{g}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2-h}-\\frac{3}{g(2-h)} & = \\\\ \\frac{5g}{g(2-h)}-\\frac{3}{g(2-h)} & = \\\\ \\frac{5g-3}{g(2-h)} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247013 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247014 13194139533689 true] [17592186247013 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247015 13194139533689 true] [17592186247013 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247016 13194139533689 true] [17592186247013 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247017 13194139533689 true] [17592186247013 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247018 13194139533689 true] [17592186247013 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533689 true] [17592186247013 1041 "selection" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247013 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247015 13194139533689 true] [17592186247013 1110 #uuid "9797a54a-5271-5c10-90e3-f81693bae428" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247014 1034 "\\frac{5g-3}{2-h}" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247014 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247014 1111 #uuid "063c2d9f-cafb-5814-b86b-b2df1f77be60" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247015 1034 "\\frac{5g-3}{g(2-h)}" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247015 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247015 1111 #uuid "05103891-f1c0-5e43-b21f-cfcad99e8e9a" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247016 1034 "\\frac{2g}{g(2-h)}" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247016 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247016 1111 #uuid "486dcd34-91c1-5c94-9581-c6240f920d57" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247017 1034 "\\frac{g-8}{g(2-h)}" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247017 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247017 1111 #uuid "3f3b28e7-9818-5e32-9ea9-e96947c7fd59" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247018 1034 "\\frac{2g}{2-h}" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247018 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247018 1111 #uuid "91805dae-6ee5-5c5e-92a2-11a11645573e" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247019 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247020 13194139533689 true] [17592186247019 1089 "q-122083" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247019 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533689 true] [17592186247019 1100 "A theme park has $5$ roller coasters, $7$ flat rides, and $3$ dark rides. How many choices are there to select a single attraction?" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247019 1113 #uuid "d3f0647c-4317-5989-96f8-e7764602d90f" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247019 1138 false 13194139533689 true] [17592186247019 1145 "In order to find the total number of choices, we can use the **rule of sum**:\n\n$$\n5+7+3=15\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $15$ choices of attractions." 13194139533689 true] [17592186247020 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247021 13194139533689 true] [17592186247020 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247022 13194139533689 true] [17592186247020 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247023 13194139533689 true] [17592186247020 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247024 13194139533689 true] [17592186247020 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247025 13194139533689 true] [17592186247020 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533689 true] [17592186247020 1041 "selection" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247020 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247024 13194139533689 true] [17592186247020 1110 #uuid "d501712c-d6c1-5660-bf9f-306a8839a4c8" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247021 1034 "12" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247021 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247021 1111 #uuid "4bc2d236-48a2-53b2-8871-f873f03741b0" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247022 1034 "10" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247022 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247022 1111 #uuid "b2c4e520-8b00-51fd-b292-7d83ec8587a0" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247023 1034 "3" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247023 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247023 1111 #uuid "d6c14c16-7a63-51e6-92c5-62b52440ab17" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247024 1034 "15" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247024 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247024 1111 #uuid "751d5ec7-b18d-55c1-89f3-66f11a9b81d0" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247025 1034 "8" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247025 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247025 1111 #uuid "0084ba1e-e56e-508c-8087-c6dadb250e3d" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247026 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247027 13194139533689 true] [17592186247026 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247029 13194139533689 true] [17592186247026 1089 "q-216936" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247026 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533689 true] [17592186247026 1100 "The midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(-9p,3q)$ and $(6p,5q)$\n is$\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247026 1113 #uuid "f6f39073-db07-5fce-998a-bd96e9d29d41" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247026 1138 false 13194139533689 true] [17592186247026 1145 "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between ${{(-9p,3q)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(6p,5q)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-9p+6p}{2},\\frac{3q+5q}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-3p}{2},\\frac{8q}{2}) \\\\  & =(-\\frac{3p}{2},4q)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247027 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247028 13194139533689 true] [17592186247027 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533689 true] [17592186247027 1041 "field-1" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247027 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247028 13194139533689 true] [17592186247027 1110 #uuid "e0933f28-6068-5bb4-8f8f-241b500b0afa" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247028 1034 "-\\frac{3p}{2}" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247028 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247028 1111 #uuid "9dc1c29a-ef88-5654-b329-b97e4b7908b5" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247029 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247030 13194139533689 true] [17592186247029 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533689 true] [17592186247029 1041 "field-2" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247029 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247030 13194139533689 true] [17592186247029 1110 #uuid "60efe028-c518-59e5-9fa7-2183f70d36a2" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247030 1034 "4q" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247030 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247030 1111 #uuid "5c806573-c998-52a7-8f19-a10c1beaedba" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247031 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247032 13194139533689 true] [17592186247031 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247034 13194139533689 true] [17592186247031 1089 "q-250552" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247031 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533689 true] [17592186247031 1100 "Solve the equation $12x={x}^{2}+61.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\pm $\n{{field-2}}$\\text{i}$" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247031 1113 #uuid "0a8f88f4-fdb0-54c4-b806-363e999f0b6c" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247031 1138 false 13194139533689 true] [17592186247031 1145 "First, we write the equation in standard form by bringing all of the terms to the left-hand side. This gives the equation\n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+12x-61=0.\n$$\n\nWe can find the roots of a quadratic equation using the quadratic formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the coefficients are $a=-1,\\,b=12,$ and $c=-61.$ Substituting these values into the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{-12\\pm \\sqrt{(12)^{2}-4(-1)(-61)}}{2(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-12\\pm \\sqrt{144-244}}{(-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-12\\pm \\sqrt{-100}}{(-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-12\\pm 10\\,\\text{i}}{(-2)} \\\\  & =6\\pm 5\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=6+5\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=6-5\\,\\text{i}.$" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247032 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247033 13194139533689 true] [17592186247032 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533689 true] [17592186247032 1041 "field-1" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247032 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247033 13194139533689 true] [17592186247032 1110 #uuid "31b4992a-0dcc-50b4-a802-4696981ed736" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247033 1034 "6" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247033 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247033 1111 #uuid "bde85d58-b17d-50a4-b7a8-2129fd3b7303" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247034 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247035 13194139533689 true] [17592186247034 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533689 true] [17592186247034 1041 "field-2" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247034 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247035 13194139533689 true] [17592186247034 1110 #uuid "a4b41d8c-17c9-51b1-8680-1a93416ea230" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247035 1034 "5" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247035 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247035 1111 #uuid "e8c28d9f-49f6-577a-9236-a526af428bf3" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247036 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247037 13194139533689 true] [17592186247036 1089 "q-276812" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247036 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533689 true] [17592186247036 1100 "The multiplicity of the root $x=5$ in the polynomial $p(x)={x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+5x+50$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533689 true] [17592186247036 1113 #uuid "1be43615-7dc6-54e4-af72-5f8d6df002b4" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247036 1138 false 13194139533689 true] [17592186247036 1145 "Since $x=5$ is a root of $p(x),$ the factor theorem tells us that $(x-5)$ is a factor of $p(x).$\n\nBecause $(x-5)$ is a factor of $p(x),$ we know that $(x-5)$ divides $p(x)$ with no remainder. So, to begin factoring $p(x),$ we can divide it by $(x-5)$ using synthetic division:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $5$ | $1$ | $-8$ | $5$ | $-50$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $5$ | $-15$ | $-50$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-3$ | $-10$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{p(x)}{x-5}={x}^{2}-3x-10,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\np(x)=(x-5)({x}^{2}-3x-10).\n$$\n\nWe can factor the quadratic factor even further, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =(x-5)(x+2)(x-5) \\\\  & =(x+2)(x-5)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $(x-5)$ has an exponent of $2$ in the factored form of $p(x).$ So the root $x=5$ has multiplicity $2.$" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247037 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247038 13194139533689 true] [17592186247037 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533689 true] [17592186247037 1041 "field-1" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247037 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247038 13194139533689 true] [17592186247037 1110 #uuid "546684cb-fc82-5ec8-97b7-93c2a7ca26eb" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247038 1034 "2" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247038 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247038 1111 #uuid "ef290df9-2242-528b-a664-cf7c14f3dfda" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247039 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247040 13194139533689 true] [17592186247039 1089 "q-31991" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247039 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533689 true] [17592186247039 1100 "Factor ${x}^{4}-{y}^{6}.$" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247039 1113 #uuid "0f67de55-0ba8-558f-bedc-a963f536e5fb" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247039 1138 false 13194139533689 true] [17592186247039 1145 "The difference of squares formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{2}-{b}^{2}=(a+b)(a-b)\n$$\n\nNotice that our expression can be written as a difference of squares:\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}-{y}^{6}={({x}^{2})}^{2}-{({y}^{3})}^{2}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor our expression using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{({x}^{2})}^{2}-{({y}^{3})}^{2}=({x}^{2}+{y}^{3})({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\n$$" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247040 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247041 13194139533689 true] [17592186247040 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247042 13194139533689 true] [17592186247040 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247043 13194139533689 true] [17592186247040 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247044 13194139533689 true] [17592186247040 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247045 13194139533689 true] [17592186247040 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533689 true] [17592186247040 1041 "selection" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247040 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247044 13194139533689 true] [17592186247040 1110 #uuid "b69a976c-9940-59c0-8642-67f7dda41156" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247041 1034 "({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247041 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247041 1111 #uuid "341fc212-577f-517c-ab67-33306cb3aaf5" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247042 1034 "({x}^{5}+{y}^{2})(x-{y}^{4})" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247042 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247042 1111 #uuid "80f4201d-4065-59f1-9bd0-41571ebb393e" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247043 1034 "({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247043 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247043 1111 #uuid "cdd5badd-26f4-5523-bca8-a89e9cc599ce" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247044 1034 "({x}^{2}+{y}^{3})({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247044 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247044 1111 #uuid "e1a01589-03f7-5932-b774-b1244389f78b" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247045 1034 "({x}^{3}+{y}^{2})({x}^{3}-{y}^{2})" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247045 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247045 1111 #uuid "418fafd4-e752-5ef6-842c-30a70989723c" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247046 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247047 13194139533689 true] [17592186247046 1089 "q-64677" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247046 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533689 true] [17592186247046 1100 "The angle $\\theta =-{210}^{∘}$ is represented in the coordinate plane in the usual way. In which quadrant does it lie?" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247046 1113 #uuid "6cc83dd4-931c-5537-b469-11f079199b4d" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247046 1138 false 13194139533689 true] [17592186247046 1145 "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $-{210}^{∘}$ by *adding* integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ until we get an angle that lies in the range $[{0}^{∘},{360}^{∘}).$\n\n- $-{210}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={150}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nSo the angle ${150}^{∘}$ is coterminal with $-{210}^{∘}.$ Let's draw this coterminal angle in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933898/assets/788edaa48306f8370f9780cdeda956a85c34b76bd6ec5a028d9d38d425cbc5b9.png)\n\nWe see that ${150}^{∘}$ lies in quadrant II. Therefore, $-{210}^{∘}$ also lies in this quadrant." 13194139533689 true] [17592186247047 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247048 13194139533689 true] [17592186247047 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247049 13194139533689 true] [17592186247047 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247050 13194139533689 true] [17592186247047 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247051 13194139533689 true] [17592186247047 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247052 13194139533689 true] [17592186247047 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533689 true] [17592186247047 1041 "selection" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247047 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247048 13194139533689 true] [17592186247047 1110 #uuid "c052030b-74d9-58a8-8736-8b235dad2028" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247048 1034 "II" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247048 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533689 true] [17592186247048 1111 #uuid "88326016-cd2e-579f-9501-d10ba9e2a358" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247049 1034 "III" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247049 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533689 true] [17592186247049 1111 #uuid "c549f1cd-e0a8-54d1-b362-a4b719321b8a" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247050 1034 "IV" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247050 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533689 true] [17592186247050 1111 #uuid "63ba62af-408d-5eb2-b367-4a240c2c02c5" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247051 1034 "Between quadrants II and III" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247051 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533689 true] [17592186247051 1111 #uuid "d2d23948-07e6-593d-b21a-96e1d46aa63e" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247052 1034 "I" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247052 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533689 true] [17592186247052 1111 #uuid "fbf15958-9625-5bfc-8f86-12089defabd4" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247053 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247054 13194139533689 true] [17592186247053 1089 "q-67703" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247053 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533689 true] [17592186247053 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933898/assets/0b0074bb582011695cec9807beab1623c6aab894e0c6abeb1bf3068be6ed3543.png)\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,3}\\frac{\\sqrt{25-f(x)}}{2}$ for the function $f(x)$ plotted above." 13194139533689 true] [17592186247053 1113 #uuid "8c978569-5523-50ca-8c37-1ccfd41ba3f3" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247053 1138 false 13194139533689 true] [17592186247053 1145 "From the graph, we get that ${lim}_{x\\to \\,3}f(x)=9.$ \n\nApplying the root rule, we get\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,3}\\frac{\\sqrt{25-f(x)}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{{lim}_{x\\to \\,3}(25-f(x))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{25-9} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\  & =2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247055 13194139533689 true] [17592186247054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247056 13194139533689 true] [17592186247054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247057 13194139533689 true] [17592186247054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247058 13194139533689 true] [17592186247054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247059 13194139533689 true] [17592186247054 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533689 true] [17592186247054 1041 "selection" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247054 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247057 13194139533689 true] [17592186247054 1110 #uuid "5517b3de-1aa8-5abb-9744-83167954beb3" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247055 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{2}" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247055 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247055 1111 #uuid "3e13b19e-6447-5793-a9d7-811cbd1772e3" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247056 1034 "-\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{2}" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247056 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247056 1111 #uuid "1643c346-9326-5da5-9021-eb40088317ab" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247057 1034 "2" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247057 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247057 1111 #uuid "7416cd0f-45b3-541c-9bcf-4a8187e34e4e" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247058 1034 "4" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247058 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533689 true] [17592186247058 1111 #uuid "dd1c17d3-aa66-5374-954d-a0b6f827ea2a" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247059 1034 "\\text{DNE}" 13194139533689 true] [17592186247059 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453